\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The lone throat is unstable; unless the seed is declared, the grid picks which way it goes. (a)~Minimal areal radius of the drainhole evolved from exact static data at refinement levels 2--4. The exact solution is a fixed point ($R_\star $, dotted); each level holds it until its own truncation error excites the unstable mode, and the fate flips with the grid: level 3 (dashed) collapses, level 4 (solid) inflates. Level 2 (grey) dies of an origin failure at $t=24.2$ (cross) with the throat still exact to $0.12\%$---too coarse to reach the branch at all. A dot marks where the \emph  {scan} loses the throat, not where the run ends: the level-3 throat is lost at $t=65$ while the run continues to $t=100$ behind a marginally trapped surface (areal radius $3.23\to 2.37$), and the muted line carries its last reading. (b)~The deviation grows exponentially on both grids: plateau fits over $t=49$--$61$ give e-fold times $\tau =5.88$ (level 3) and $5.26$ (level 4)---the same unstable mode to $9\%$, $T=\tau \,\alpha _{\rm  th}/R_\star =0.87$ and $0.78$ against the Gonz\'alez--Guzm\'an--Sarbach band $0.68$--$0.76$~\cite  {gonzalez2009}---with opposite sign. The fate is the truncation seed's; the mode is the throat's. (c)~The same throat at one resolution (level 3) with the seed \emph  {declared}, under the kick of Eq.~\eqref  {eq:seed}: $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ (heavy), $\pm 10^{-3}$ (light); dashed = outward ($\varepsilon >0$). The fate is opposite to the push, and each pair crosses itself at the $\varepsilon $-independent $t_\times \simeq 13.0$---linear response. Burgundy: exponential fits $|R-R_\star |\propto e^{t/\tau }$, $\tau =4.5$ ($t=18$--$31$) and $4.0$ ($t=16$--$26$)---steeper than the unkicked mode of (b) while the kick's transient decays. Cross: death at $t=40.1$. The $\varepsilon =+10^{-2}$ arm holds a horizon from $t=11$ (areal radius $3.88\to 2.34\to 2.57$) and runs clean to $t=100$; its muted line is again a stalled radius, not a stopped run. A tenfold smaller kick arrives $8$--$12$ units later.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:single_throat}{{1}{4}{The lone throat is unstable; unless the seed is declared, the grid picks which way it goes. (a)~Minimal areal radius of the drainhole evolved from exact static data at refinement levels 2--4. The exact solution is a fixed point ($R_\star $, dotted); each level holds it until its own truncation error excites the unstable mode, and the fate flips with the grid: level 3 (dashed) collapses, level 4 (solid) inflates. Level 2 (grey) dies of an origin failure at $t=24.2$ (cross) with the throat still exact to $0.12\%$---too coarse to reach the branch at all. A dot marks where the \emph {scan} loses the throat, not where the run ends: the level-3 throat is lost at $t=65$ while the run continues to $t=100$ behind a marginally trapped surface (areal radius $3.23\to 2.37$), and the muted line carries its last reading. (b)~The deviation grows exponentially on both grids: plateau fits over $t=49$--$61$ give e-fold times $\tau =5.88$ (level 3) and $5.26$ (level 4)---the same unstable mode to $9\%$, $T=\tau \,\alpha _{\rm th}/R_\star =0.87$ and $0.78$ against the Gonz\'alez--Guzm\'an--Sarbach band $0.68$--$0.76$~\cite {gonzalez2009}---with opposite sign. The fate is the truncation seed's; the mode is the throat's. (c)~The same throat at one resolution (level 3) with the seed \emph {declared}, under the kick of Eq.~\eqref {eq:seed}: $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ (heavy), $\pm 10^{-3}$ (light); dashed = outward ($\varepsilon >0$). The fate is opposite to the push, and each pair crosses itself at the $\varepsilon $-independent $t_\times \simeq 13.0$---linear response. Burgundy: exponential fits $|R-R_\star |\propto e^{t/\tau }$, $\tau =4.5$ ($t=18$--$31$) and $4.0$ ($t=16$--$26$)---steeper than the unkicked mode of (b) while the kick's transient decays. Cross: death at $t=40.1$. The $\varepsilon =+10^{-2}$ arm holds a horizon from $t=11$ (areal radius $3.88\to 2.34\to 2.57$) and runs clean to $t=100$; its muted line is again a stalled radius, not a stopped run. A tenfold smaller kick arrives $8$--$12$ units later}{figure.1}{}}
